<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    English (en-US) — the source language. This unqualified values/ folder is both the English
    copy and the fallback for any key a translation has not covered yet, so nothing here may be
    deleted just because a translated file exists.

    To add a language, copy this file to values-<code>/strings.xml (values-fr, values-de,
    values-hi, values-pt-rBR …) and translate the values only — never the name attributes. AGP
    regenerates the locale config from the folders that exist, so the language then appears in
    Android 13+'s per-app language picker with no further wiring.

    Leave a key out of a translation and English is used for it; lint's MissingTranslation check
    reports those once a second locale exists.
-->
